# Line endings are pinned so a checkout does not depend on the machine's
# core.autocrlf setting. Two reasons, both learned the hard way:
#   * scripts/bump.ps1 parses repo files with ^...$ anchored .NET regexes, and
#     .NET's $ does not match before CRLF -- a CRLF checkout (autocrlf=true,
#     the Git for Windows default and what GitHub's Windows runners do) made
#     the release pipeline abort with "version field not found"
#   * the release scripts are shared by a local machine and CI, and "works
#     here, CRLF there" is not a difference worth debugging twice
#
# Everything is stored as LF in the index already, so this changes no content
# -- only how a checkout materialises.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch, never diff as text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
